10:06:33   5. WHERE CONDITIONS MOVE THE ODDS - a preview of the conditional tables (Phase C)
10:06:33      LIFT = (realised - baseline) in the group, minus the same miss over ALL rows of that
10:06:33      year - so a drift that lifts every group at once (a bull year, cheaper trades) is
10:06:33      taken out and only what the condition adds is left. Percentage points. Listed only
10:06:33      when the lift has the SAME sign in all three years AND its 90% interval excludes 0.
10:06:33      A lift is a candidate, not a forecast: Phase C has to turn it into one and beat the
10:06:33      baseline out of sample, with a penalty for how many candidates were looked at.
10:06:33      38 of 288 condition groups met both tests. By chance alone about 22 would
10:06:33      (90% range 14-29); more than that suggests some structure is real, but not WHICH rows.
